In article <1991Oct24.135217.11547@phillip.edu.au> rkummer@phillip.edu.au writes:
>
>upgrading a PDP-11/73 running RSX11M version 4.1 .My probelm is that if I
>switch off or disconnect the terminal connected to TT0: which is setup as the
>console terminal, then the system crashes. If it is possible to do so, how can
>I reconfigure the system so that I can switch off the console terminal, or
>disconnect it completely without these problems? 
>Any help would be much appreciated, thanks.

You probably have a DLV11j or equivalent board in the system.  It contains
a jumper for choosing the action to take when receiving a break from the
console device (csr=177560-566).  The choices are usually halt, reboot or
ignore.  It may be a jumper or a switch dependant on the maker of the
device.  If you can identify the board the console is connected to, someone
here can probably look up the correct setting.

Shutting off a terminal tends to send break-like message to the console.


