Having just received my copy of the DEC Professional Annual buyers guide, 
I glanced through the section on laser printers - Some of the larger ones
(noticably Rosetta Technologies, Advanced Technologies, Dataproducts, and 
others) have monthly duty cycles in excess of 100K - 150K pages. Also mentioned
is the paper input capacity ranging from 750 to 2000 pages - the review does 
not go into detail on cycling between trays.
  Depending on your needs, you may also want to consider an ion deposition 
printer, as they are build as production machines. Some of them do 45 ppm,
have +40 resident fonts and a +250k monthly duty cycle.
  If you need them I can send you a list of their names + numbers - thats
if you can't get a copy of the DEC Pro guide....


