We use a DECSYSTEM 5500 (64 Mb memory, 6 x rz57) as a server (dms) for 24
stations (3100, 5000/120/125/200) and as an interactive compute server (fortran,
development, Mathematica, IDL, mail, NEWS etc.). 30 to 40 interactive users
during working hours. Background jobs (4 to 8) run under NQS. System is
operational for 9 months now.

Performance is very good. No problems with response time. SCSI disks are
not very fast, but the prestoserve increases NFS performance significantly.

Install as much memory you can get. CPU performance should not give any
problems but paging/swapping can decrease performance.

Good luck, Henk
