> that I press the load button on each drive. On both drives the load lights
> go off. A few seconds later, so do the fault lights. Then the ready lights 
> come on it. I've also tried variatons of starting the PDP before the drives.
> They all end up the same way though.  Also, I noticed that if I press 
> <CNTL> BOOT on the PDP, the fault light flashes on drive 0, the ready light
> clicks off for a second and so does the drive 1 ready light. the drives make
> a clicking sound and then both ready lights come back on.  This happens 
> regaudless to the address I am at on the machine.  Aside from this, I can't
> get the PDP to do anything. Any suggestions? Helpful hints? RT-11 user's 
> manuals, etc?  Thanks in advance. 

  The RL02 drive has no intelligence to speak of. The buttons are sensed by
the controller, which then updates the lamps. If the controller isn't running
the default is to put the lamps on (except for Write Protect, which is wired
internally to the drive). When you power up the CPU, the controller initial-
izes and updates the lamps. When you do a bus init on the CPU, it does the
same thing.

  What console and emulation ROM do you have in the '34? If you get a bunch
of hex output on the console TTY (4 groups of numbers) followed by an @-sign,
your machine boots by typing DM<CR> (caps required) on the console TTY. If
it doesn't do that, it either has power-up boot set to some device or it's
broken. Use the front panel (if you have one) to examine the following lo-
cations:

765774, 773000, 773200, 773400, 773600

  Send me mail and tell me what you get and I can give you more help. In the
meantime, one of the 773x00 addresses should have an 042114 in it - that is
the RL02 bootstrap. When you find it, start the CPU at the address + 4 - for
example, if you find it at 773200, start the CPU at 773204 and it'll boot the
first RL02 drive.

