Andy,

In the cover letter for VMS V5.4-3 DEC states:

				CAUTION

VAXcluster software Version 5.4-3 does not support the DEQNA device.  Do not
install VMS Version V5.4-3 if a node in your cluster is connected through the
DEQNA....

Later in the letter:

DEQNA Support
VMS Version 5.4-3 local area VAXcluster software does not support the DEQNA
Q-bus to Ethernet adapter.  If a node in your cluster is connected through the
DEQNA device, you must replace the DEQNA with a DELQA or a DESQA BEFORE
UPDATING to VMS Version 5.4-3.  Contact your Digital Representative for
information about the DEQNA upgrade program.

DECNET-VAX still supports the DEQNA device.  Digital recommends that you
replace your DEQNA now, however, because the NEXT RELASE of the VMS operating
system will withdraw ALL SUPPORT for the DEQNA...

So if you do not intend to go to VMS V5.4-3 or later you will still be able to
use your DEQNA.  Since the cover letter talks about the DEQNA upgrade program I
suppose that that program is still going on (for now).

