>If you're using smail 2.5, you shouldn't need to do *anything* with sendmail.cf
>since it's perfectly capable of replacing sendmail completely, with a little
>help from "deliver" or my "router" program.

I took the original request to mean that the cluster of DECstations
were connected by TCP/IP/SMTP etc.  Smail 2.5 won't do that.
In such a configuration, you usually replace the "uux" delivery
clause in the sendmail.cf with an invocation of smail, so that smail
only does UUCP delivery.  The Smail 2.5 docs seem to cover it fairly
throughly, but I've never done it, and some vendor's sendmail.cf's are
thoroughly f**ked w.r.t. UUCP handling.
