>To get back to the beginning of this discussion, I was reading the KDJ11-B
>module users guide, and in the configuration part, it mentions a jumper (W20),
>that, if installed indicates that this module is a single processor. 
>I assume that if you remove it, it indicates that it is a multiple processor?
>
>   What is/was that going to be used for??

It sounds like it connects the bus arbitration circuitry. Unit
processors usually have the bus head-end circuit on the processor;
symmetric multi's must either have a distributed system, or have it on
the backplane.
