Just a couple bits of trivia discovered late last evening.

In anticipation of the day when tape drives can be shared cluster-wide,
I had configured our 3400's TK70 drive as unit 1.  (The unit number is
set on the TKQ70 controller's jumper block closest to the EPROMs; the
jumper on this block furthest from the EPROM is the unit number's LSB.)
This configuration works fine for VMS 5.4-2 and Standalone Backup
operations, and the device appears as it should from a console
SHOW DEVICE command.  This configuration fails however for
the console BOOT MUA1 command, which results in:

  ?4B CTRLERR MUA1

which I would bet somewhere translates to "unit not available" or some such
rot.  Reconfiguring as unit 0 makes everyone happy.  Somehow it wouldn't
suprise me if the KA640 CPU's 188/189E7 (and beyond?) firmware can't
handle anything other than MUx0 when BOOTing from a TK70.

