	Chris,

	  The video cable actually is the least of your problems (depending
	upon your definition of convenient). The first thing that you need
	to think about is what distance you are trying to maintain? If you
	are under 10' you should have no problems (that I know of). If you
	are under 20' it will still probably work. Longer than that you are
	probably going to have to use a repeater box of some sort. 

	  The video issue is pretty tightly tied to the signal that we take
	our synch from. In the color monitors you can be reasonably certain
	that they synch on green (that is that the refresh rate of the monitor
	is matched by the green video output).

	  The problem for the keyboard and mouse cables will just be the
	signal attenuation and you'll undoubtedly have video problems first.

	  Anyway, you can order cables direct from DEC (you just don't know
	it and neither do most of us). The BC19S (10' color video cable for
	the VS3100 with a list of ~$80) will work for the DS2100/DS3100 units.
	One of my colleagues down the hall has been successfully running such
	a configuration for over 18 months. The cable is NOT qualified on
	the DS2100/DS3100 so you'll have to take your chances there. Also,
	you can't plug the keyboard and mouse cables into the video connector
	on the cable. If the keyboard and mouse cables don't connect to the
	back of the box then the system will fault.

	
	  And before anybody sends me mail about longer cables for the DS5000
	series machines (DS5000/200,DS5000/1xx), yes it IS possible to do. It
	has been done for a couple of customers. But again, non of this has
