I don't recall seeing an 8085 in a -220 when I opened it up; I do recall
seeing an 8051, though. As far as the DECmate goes, my DECmate II has:
	- 6120 PDP-8 compatible CPU
	- Z80 CP/M coprocessor
	- 8051 hard disk controller
	- 8051 floppy controller
	- ???? in the keyboard
The fun thing about this is that whenever CP/M wants to read a disk, it
asks the PDP-8 which forwards the request to an 8051, which does the read
and passes the data back to the PDP-8, which passes the data back to the
Z80.

