Unibus peripherals onto a '15.  This one had RK11/RK05 drives.  It was used on
a wind tunnel.

If I remember rightly,...... 
    the RK11 had a strap somewhere to change it from 16 to 18 bit data - I'm
    not sure how they squeezed 18 bits thru' 16 lines though.  (Unibus has 18
    address lines, but only 16 data lines).  The 16 bit strap made it an RK11D
    (standard PDP11) and the other way made it an RK11E, 18 bit. 

