Disclaimer first: these are my personal opinions alone, and do not reflect any
position of Mentec Computer Systems.

Firstly we got into the PDP-11 business around 1982. We now have an installed
base of something over 10,000 PDP-11 processor boards in the field, mostly
in embedded systems with major european multi-nationals. We started shipping
our original M70 series in 1986 and the M90 series product in 1988. The M90
has therefore been around quite a while and I reckon the PDP 11/93-94
looks kinda like something we have been shipping for three years.

Further Bruce McCully (mcculley@racy.zko.dec.com) writes:

> I haven't tested the Mentec products, nor do I know anyone in the corporation
> who has.  So that is only an assumption about the correctness of their system
> design.  Based on my experience with other products, I tend to regard any such
> assumptions as unlikely to be entirely true.  The question is to what degree and
> in what regard is total correctness of design violated, and does that cause any
> visible and objectionable symptoms to the user.  Different users might have
> different views on that...
.
.
.
> I spent over a year testing the KDJ11-E (both before and after introduction)
>  and know that there were a couple of problems in that area which have been
> fixed.  I would tend to be very cautious about any board of comparable
> complexity and perfomance which I did not know to have had testing as
> rigorous as I know the KDJ11-E to have endured, but that's just my opinion.
>  Your mileage may vary...

I worked on the design and design verification testing of the M90.
I cannot claim that the M90 design is totally correct, what I can however say
is that at this point, after extensive design verification testing, beta site
testing, and large numbers of units in the field we know of no design errors,
nothing that makes system generation for RSX,RSTS,RT-11,DSM etc any different
for an M90, or any other substantial difference except for the setup and 
bootstrap, but we could hardly use DEC copyrighted code for that.

> I have no knowledge that would allow me to form an opinion about the performance
> of the Mentec board.  I do know that the KDJ11-E has a very significant increase
