 One of our engineers (who had extensive PDP-11/RSX-11M+ experience) was
 at the Colorado CSC recently and actually SAW the 11/74 at work. It
 still lives albeit well hidden. I have also hear rumors that it never
 really saw the light of day because of the threat to the VAX world. If
 you examine the RSX-11M+ manual set you will find many blue entries for
 error messages (for instance) that refer to RSX-11M+ multiprocessor
 systems. Example: in the MCR commands section, an ABO error message
 "Required bus runs are offline or not present" means (RSX-11M+
 multiprocessor systems only) The task, or a common that the task is
 mapped to, was installed with an affinity for a CPU or a bus run that
 is offline. the OPE command under MCR has a keyword "/CPU=CPx" which
 "Accesses an address relative to the specified CPU partition.       

 Just glance through looking for the light blue entries to see what
 might have been possible.
