> *age*, and TeX reports that it's reading:

Are the files in an UCX *container* or are the files shared ? 
I have had problems with such a low performance in a directory 
where I had about 1000 files. Even VMS takes its time. The workaround 
was to set up a directory on UNIX with soft links to the UCX NFS disk. This 
resulted in a (local) fast 'ls' on UNIX, and only in case where the file 
was actually be accessed the link retrieved the correct file via nfs. The 
only bothering thing is that each time you change a file in this 
directory you need to rerun the procedure creating the soft links. However, 
because this was a database as your tex fonts, I consider it to be a 
small side-effect and not a problem. 

