I was wondering how other admin people feel about
the utility scamp.  We have a couple of DECstations
and a DECsystem among 4 other Unix platforms.  Each
of these are running Ultrix 4.2.  Included with 4.2
is an ATTEMPT at system admin tool called scamp.

I would have to say that this took all of about 1
day to write.  The functionality of this tool is a
joke in comparison to their competitors.  If anyone
has used smit (IBM), sam (HP), or sysadm (DG) you know
what I am talking about.  My personal favorite is sysadm
on the new DG/UX 5.4, though sam on HP/UX 8.0 is better
now too.

User accounting is limited to adding and removing a user,
thats it!  What happened to groups, and mail aliases, ...
If you go in to network set-up it just contains a blurb
on what you should be thinking about and thats it! There is
no options but just read a README. I could go on, ...1

This thing even comes with its own manual, what for?
Most people are maintaining a hetergeneous environment
with many parameters, the need for a full-functional system
tool is advantage for many of us to get a work done the fast,
efficient, and along the idiosyncrasies that each vendor
imposes on each of their Unix implementations.

Sorry for the bandwidth, but this is so far behind the similar
tools of HP, IBM, and DG that I feel DEC should really make
a concerted effort in totally redesiging this tool and including
it in their next release as soon as possible.  What do they have
to say in their defense?
