In article <kf2rbjINNhd9@grapevine> smckinty@sunicnc.France.Sun.COM (Steve McKinty - Sun ICNC) writes:
>In article <1991Oct7.215253.22597@mnemosyne.cs.du.edu>, aduell@isis.cs.du.edu (Tony Duell) writes:
>
>Some years ago I remember reading that DEC had a multiprocessor PDP/11
>running in their Labs. It had 4 CPU's and was running a variant of RSX11.
>It never saw the light of day, I guess multiprocessor VAXen overshadowed
>it.
>   > 
>
