That was the 11/74 which briefly (supposedly) went into alpha or beta outside
DEC.  It was from 1 to 4 11/70's with shared memory.  This is where the MK11
MOS memory system was originally supposed to be used.  The MK11 was retrofitted
to the 11/70's later.

The machine had a modified backplane with different cache and memory management
and a board called the IST (some kind of sanity timer which [rumour said]
would sound a sonalert on the failed CPU.

The suckers ran at DEC for years.  DEC developed and built their RSX masters on
this one.  I had 1/4 of one at DEC Princeton.  DEC put it there when they needed
11/70's for AT&T and were unable to build any.

It supposedly ran faster than 11/780's.


