> I need some explanations on this one. I want to get some DECnet packets
>from a VAX sitting on an ethernet with a CISCO , which is connected to an
>X.25 network.
OK, here's what you do.

You need to connect an additional serial line between the VAX and cisco, and
then use X.25 switching to route calls from your X.25 network to the VAX. On
the VAX, you need to enable routing, and have it route between the serial interface
and the ethernet.

This will allow any of your remote VAX systems to place X.25 calls "through" the cisco
into the local VAX. The local VAX can then route the traffic on to the ethernet, giving
the remote VAX systems full connectivity.

Does this help you?

Kevin


